---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture Overview"
  description="High-level SensOS product architecture: observe, understand, control — without model weight changes."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Overview</p>
    <h1>Architecture</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      SensOS is an observation-centered runtime safety platform. Public materials
      describe product behavior and interface contracts — not internal kernels.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/rfc">Public Standards</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/developer">Developer Docs</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/enterprise">Enterprise</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 48rem;">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Observe</strong> — continuously watch AI runtime behavior.</li>
      <li><strong>Understand</strong> — detect semantic trajectory risk.</li>
      <li><strong>Control</strong> — intervene safely without changing model weights.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 48rem;">
    <h2>What is published</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Public ABIs and interoperability guarantees</li>
      <li>Conformance expectations</li>
      <li>Constitutional roles and responsibility boundaries</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">
      Detailed topology graphs, internal module maps, and execution strategies are
      not part of the public site.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
